b58f3852cf9a57af1a0beae857e8d92dc02094332f7029c823","file":"preprints/Sharp-One-Dimensional-Lieb-Thirring-Constants-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":37,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e2dc7068e4df6e05c0bbc175a77bdb68f4bb79af174e8d432b137d663450d318","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Sharp-One-Dimensional-Lieb-Thirring-Constants-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:31de33d78a2044b58f3852cf9a57af1a0beae857e8d92dc02094332f7029c823","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Sharp-One-Dimensional-Lieb-Thirring-Constants-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L37"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every $1/2<\\gamma<3/2$ and every nonnegative\n$W\\in L^{\\gamma+1/2}(\\R)$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\Tr(H_{-W})_-^\\gamma\n \\le 2\\left(\\frac{\\gamma-1/2}{\\gamma+1/2}\\right)^{\\gamma-1/2}\n       L_{\\gamma,1}^{\\cl}\\int_\\R W^{\\gamma+1/2}.\n\\end{equation}\nThe constant is optimal and equals $L_{\\gamma,1}^{(1)}$.\nMore precisely, if $r=(\\gamma-1/2)^{-1}$, equality is attained by\n$W(x)=(r+1)\\sech^2(rx)$."}
